      "title": "L&T Technology Services, Nokia sign deal to support engineering in India",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/l-t-technology-services-nokia-announce-engineering-collaboration-126102600363_1.html",
      "description": "L&amp;T Technology Services on Monday announced a five-year contract with Nokia to support engineering and research and development activities in India.\nThe contract brings together LTTS' engineering capabilities with Nokia's telecommunications technology work, according to a release.\nThe release did not divulge the size or financial details of the contract.\nUnder the agreement, LTTS will support Nokia R&amp;D programs across areas, including product engineering, software development, system integration, and product support.\nLTTS will establish a dedicated Offshore Development Center (ODC) in India to support Nokia's engineering and R&amp;D initiatives.\nThe ODC brings data-center-grade compute and AI-infrastructure engineering to next-generation telecom solutions.\nLTTS will also create a dedicated engineering team in India to support Nokia's technology center globally, with work spanning areas such as 5G networks, intelligent automation, AI-driven operations and AI ...",
